ic anal fissures may require more extensive treatment, such as:\n\n* Lateral internal sphincterotomy (LIS): A surgical procedure that cuts the internal anal sphincter muscle to relieve pressure and promote healing.\n* Fissurectomy: A minor surgical procedure to repair the tear or cut in the anal canal lining.\n\nIn summary, while both hemorrhoids and fissures can be managed conservatively, the likelihood of complete spontaneous resolution varies. Hemorrhoids may require additional treatment, whereas acute anal fissures typically heal on their own with proper care.	f	\N
