1033	62	9	\N	No, the **stomach flu** and the **flu (influenza)** are **not the same**, though they share some overlapping symptoms.\n\n- **Stomach flu** is **not caused by influenza** but typically refers to **viral gastroenteritis**, most commonly caused by **norovirus** or **rotavirus**. It primarily affects the **digestive system**, causing:\n  - Nausea, vomiting, diarrhea\n  - Stomach cramps\n  - Low-grade fever (sometimes)\n\n- **Influenza (the flu)** is a **respiratory illness** caused by **influenza viruses (A, B, or C)**. It mainly affects the **lungs and airways**, leading to:\n  - Fever, chills, muscle aches\n  - Cough, sore throat, congestion\n  - Fatigue (often severe)\n\n**Key Difference:** The flu rarely causes **severe vomiting/diarrhea**, while stomach flu rarely causes **severe respiratory symptoms**.\n\n**Treatment:** Both are usually self-limiting, but hydration is critical for stomach flu, while antiviral meds (e.g., Tamiflu) may help influenza if taken early.	t	\N
