1049	62	11	\N	No, the stomach flu and the flu are not the same thing. The stomach flu is a colloquial term for viral gastroenteritis, which is an inflammation of the stomach and intestines, typically caused by norovirus, rotavirus, or other viruses. It leads to symptoms like nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and stomach cramps. The flu, or influenza, is caused by the influenza virus and primarily affects the respiratory system, leading to symptoms such as fever, cough, sore throat, and body aches. While both can cause gastrointestinal symptoms, they are caused by different viruses and have distinct clinical presentations.	t	\N
